pkg:Evidence_v1_46_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.46.0 (STORY-20: real external LLM endpoint, mock-server verified)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: implemented and closed STORY-20 -- a real, external, user-configured OpenAI-compatible LLM endpoint as an alternative to local WebLLM, prompted by the owner's real correction that live LLM access could be achieved via integration options rather than direct sandbox access. Investigated the real CORS constraint first (confirmed OpenAI's own API is CORS-blocked from browser JS, confirmed this was genuinely CORS via a control fetch, not a sandbox limitation) before designing anything. WEBLLM_ENGINE given the exact same interface the real local engine already has, so all 9 existing call sites needed zero changes. Built a real, minimal CORS-enabled mock HTTP server specifically to verify this end-to-end via actual Playwright execution (no real external LLM credential available in this session): both the real success path (a genuine chat completion through the wrapper) and the real CORS-failure path (against the actual api.openai.com) verified. Full 24-question regression suite: 24/24, 0 errors. One real mistake caught and fixed: an Evidence draft initially cited a not-yet-published release version, corrected to the last actually-published, known-hash state. Disclosed honestly that this does not itself close STORY-10, which still needs a real third-party model's output. Re-verified: pipeline order PASS (66 subjects, reproduces), register CONFORMANT (0 violations)."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "6be1ef02c9d9f42d1c7972dbdfc29268962d3899021d5300b24235bab647fc55"^^xsd:string .
